queues work, or rejects it. Then explain how operators detect the condition and how the system returns to

26
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:57,450
normal. For every major component, connect the choice to a requirement and name the cost it introduces. A

27
00:05:57,500 --> 00:06:11,200
cache reduces latency but creates freshness and invalidation work. Replication improves resilience and read capacity but introduces lag,

28
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:24,950
conflict, and failover decisions. Partitioning increases scale but complicates queries, transactions, and rebalancing. Asynchronous work absorbs bursts but

29
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:38,700
changes completion semantics and requires retries, deduplication, and backlog operations. This requirement-choice-cost pattern keeps the answer grounded and

30
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:52,450
prevents architecture by buzzword. Start with the

31
00:06:52,500 --> 00:07:06,200
simplest architecture that satisfies the stated scale. Then identify the first bottleneck and evolve one dimension at a

32
00:07:06,250 --> 00:07:19,950
